    "details": "<p><strong>Koolage Cybersecurity Challenge</strong></p>\n<p>Think you can spot a security vulnerability before an attacker does?</p>\n<p>Join the <strong>Koolage Cybersecurity Challenge</strong> and test your understanding of real-world application security.</p>\n<p>Participants will encounter practical cybersecurity scenarios involving:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Web Application Security</li>\n<li>Authentication &amp; Authorization</li>\n<li>API Security</li>\n<li>Common Vulnerabilities</li>\n<li>Security Analysis</li>\n<li>Cybersecurity Problem Solving</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What You'll Learn</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>How common web vulnerabilities work</li>\n<li>How to identify security weaknesses</li>\n<li>How authentication differs from authorization</li>\n<li>How APIs can introduce security risks</li>\n<li>How security professionals approach vulnerability analysis</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who Can Participate?</strong></p>\n<p>Open to students and cybersecurity enthusiasts interested in:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Cybersecurity</li>\n<li>Ethical Hacking</li>\n<li>VAPT</li>\n<li>Web Security</li>\n<li>API Security</li>\n<li>Application Security</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>No advanced experience is required.</strong> Students with a basic understanding of cybersecurity are welcome.</p>\n<p><strong>Challenge Format</strong></p>\n<p>Participants will solve a series of cybersecurity-based questions and scenarios designed to test <strong>knowledge, analytical thinking, and problem-solving ability</strong>.</p>",
